    {
      "id": "reg-m2-tbs2-ex1",
      "title": "Credit agreements",
      "html": "<p>Both lenders gave value and obtained valid security agreements covering debtor-owned equipment. A filed and perfected on January 5; B filed and perfected on February 10. No priority exception applies.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "reg-m2-tbs2-ex2",
      "title": "Bankruptcy event",
      "html": "<p>The debtor later files a petition that triggers an automatic stay. B proposes immediately seizing the equipment without evaluating relief or exceptions. A junior analyst states that discharge always removes every lien.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "explanation": "<h3>Concept supported by value, debtor rights, and valid agreement</h3><p>These are core attachment elements under the assumed rules.</p><h3>Ordinary priority under the given facts</h3><p>A has the earlier qualifying filing/perfection date.</p><h3>Response to B’s proposed seizure</h3><p>The stay constrains collection activity.</p><h3>Correct the analyst’s statement</h3><p>Bankruptcy protections and exceptions are not universal cancellation rules.</p>"
